   "unmapped": [
    "Reward function evolves via Gauss-Markov model f_{t+1} = sqrt(1-eps) f_t + sqrt(eps) g_{t+1}, g_t ~ GP(0,k) i.i.d.; eps is known to the learner",
    "Kernel k with k(x,x) <= 1 and tail conditions on sup|f| and its derivatives",
    "Domain D subset [0,r]^d compact convex"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "f_1(x) = g_1(x), f_{t+1}(x) = \\sqrt{1 - \\epsilon}\\,f_{t}(x) +  \\sqrt{\\epsilon}\\,g_{t+1}(x) ... the instantaneous regret we incur at time t is r_t = f_t(x^*_t) - f_t(x_t). We are interested in minimizing the cumulative regret R_T = \\sum_{t=1}^T r_t."
  },
